// ?aptHelper008AE3A0@@YAPAVAptValue@@PAXHH@Z
// partial score=0.9819 date=2026-09-29
// cl: /O2 /Ob1 /DNDEBUG /DWIN32 /D_WINDOWS /MD
//
// Byte status: 166 of 166 bytes (size-exact), shape 1.000 once registers and
// constants are normalised; 3 non-reloc bytes differ, all at the SECOND
// bit-15 test (+0x47):
//   retail  +0047 c1 ea 0f / +004a f6 d2    / +004c f6 c2 01  (shr edx,0xf / not dl / test dl,1 / jne)
//   ours    +0047 c1 ea 07 / +004a f7 d2    / +004c f6 c6 01  (shr edx,7   / not edx / test dh,1 / jne)
// Polarity (jne to the toInteger path) and every other instruction in the
// 166-byte body match byte-for-byte, including the shared exit, the goto
// fallback, the xor/and/xor bit-25 RMW of owner+0x1c, and the setne/shl
// bitfield assignment for m_flag.
//
// Semantics (machine-checked over 200k random + edge flag words):
//   ((~((v) >> 7) & 0x100) == 0)  <=>  ((v >> 15) & 1) == 1,
// i.e. the bfmeGo1034F path is taken iff bit15 is set, exactly as retail's
// shr/not/test sequence tests. The shift-7/mask-0x100 spelling reads the same
// bit through dh instead of dl; it is unusual but behaviour-identical.
//
// Why not the natural spelling: every `(~((v) >> 15) & 1)`-family form that
// is bit15-correct (with ~, uchar casts, hoisted locals, named kind locals,
// conjunction vs nesting, plain-struct vs union reads) makes MSVC 7.1 park
// the flags word in esi (push esi / mov esi,[ecx+4] / mov edx,esi, plus
// knock-on edi juggling in the tail), landing at 171-172 bytes. Every form
// that keeps retail's edx allocation either folds the test (160-162 bytes:
// test dh,dh, with or without a surviving `not edx`) or tests a different
// bit. Mask-width sweep: masks confined to the low byte always spill;
// masks touching dh or higher fit. Narrowing the ~ to byte width (uchar,
// ushort, inner casts, volatile) spills, folds, or widens the test.
// ~60 spellings measured this session; see 0x008ae3a0_alternatives/README.md.
// The 3-byte residue (shift imm, not width, test register) looks like one
// compiler-internal allocation choice with no remaining source-level lever;
// shape_family_levers over all ten families previously reported no lever.
//
// 2026-09-30: the mechanism behind the 6 bytes is identified and is NOT a
// spelling problem. Any low-byte `~`-and-test of `last`'s flags word shares one
// expression tree with the kind mask, so MSVC 7.1 promotes the load to a
// long-lived local, allocates a callee-saved register for it and copies twice
// (171-172 B) - that family is the only one that emits retail's exact
// `shr edx,0xf / not dl / test dl,1`. When the two reads are provably
// different addresses nothing is live across the kind test, the second load is
// rematerialised straight into the shift register and the site bytes come out
// exact at 166-167 B; a type-punned read of the CORRECT offset re-CSEs and
// falls back to the spill. Retail's arrangement is a 3-byte load plus a 2-byte
// reg-to-reg copy, and MSVC will not build it for this expression, so 167 B is
// the floor for the family. ~70 further spellings, plus
// shape_family_levers over all ten families on this bank ("no applicable
// source-level family lever"), all measured; see the README's 2026-09-30
// section and the sweep drivers kept beside it.
//
// Provenance of the reconstruction (all cited in targets/game/reverse/symbols.csv
// row 15555 and the two landed neighbour wrappers):
//   - callers 0x008AE450 and 0x008AE470 pass (entry, count, flag); the body
//     reads all three args and returns the AptValue fallback pointer.
//   - 0x008D3280 is matched BfmeF1034::bfmeGo1034F; 0x00898300 is matched
//     AptValue::toInteger; 0x008D2130 remains a dump, declared __thiscall void
//     per tools/callees.py (result unused at every site).
//   - EA source file per the brief: Libraries/Source/Apt/AptCharacter.cpp.
// The name is the address-derived pin already in symbols.csv; no vtable slot,
// emitter or named caller proves a real owning symbol, so it is not upgraded.
// The m_bit15 union member records the witnessed bit position (both retail
// test sequences isolate bit15); the emitted test currently reads m_value
// because the bitfield form folds.

class AptValue
{
public:
	int toInteger() const;
};

class BfmeF1034
{
public:
	int bfmeGo1034F(int key);
